  "body": "Brimming with charm, warmth, and timeless appeal, this beautiful 1930s home has a wonderful villa feel, with high ceilings, a charming bay window and character features that give it a sense of space and enduring elegance. Thoughtfully renovated to blend classic character with contemporary comfort, this is coastal living at its best in the heart of Manly.\r\n\r\nSet on a generous 600sqm freehold site, the home enjoys a sunny north-facing aspect, with a large deck providing the perfect setting for relaxed afternoons, entertaining friends, and family, or simply soaking up the sunshine.\r\nThe updated kitchen and bathrooms bring a fresh, modern feel while preserving the home's charm. With four bedrooms and three bathrooms, there is plenty of room for families to spread out and enjoy.\r\nAdding exceptional versatility is the completely private, self-contained accommodation downstairs, featuring a separate double bedroom, bathroom, lounge, and kitchen. Whether you need space for extended family, independent teenage living, visiting guests or an additional income opportunity, this separate space offers plenty of options.\r\nA single internal-access garage and additional off-street parking complete the package.\r\nEnjoy an easy stroll to Little Manly Beach, with coastal walks, cafés, shops and everyday essentials close by. Families will also appreciate being in zone for both Whangaparaoa Primary School and Whangaparaoa College.\r\n\r\nProperty highlights:\r\n1.\tBeautiful 1930s-character home with a charming villa feel\r\n2.\tHigh ceilings and an attractive bay window\r\n3.\tFour bedrooms and three bathrooms\r\n4.\tBeautifully refreshed kitchen and bathrooms\r\n5.\tHuge storage area under the house\r\n6.\tHealthy homes compliant\r\n7.\tPrivate, self-contained downstairs accommodation with double bedroom, bathroom, lounge and kitchen plus its own off-street carpark\r\n8.\tSunny north-facing aspect and large entertaining deck\r\n9.\tGenerous 600sqm freehold site\r\n10.\tSingle internal-access garage plus off-street parking\r\n11.\tEasy walking distance to Little Manly Beach and shops\r\n12.\tZoned for Whangaparaoa Primary School and Whangaparaoa College\r\n\r\nWhether you're searching for a welcoming family home, space for extended family or the added versatility of self-contained accommodation, this Manly beauty delivers a lifestyle opportunity not to be missed.\r\n\r\nTo view/download the property documents use the following link: https://www.harcourtsfiles.co.nz/listings/SLM1\r\n\r\nFor viewings, please attend one of the scheduled open homes. This property is to be sold by Deadline Sale on the 18th November at 4.00pm (unless sold prior).",
